# alias: OppsPreempt4M
# button-text: Opps Preempt 4M
# gib-works: true
# bba-works: true
# auction-filter: Auction.....\n4[HS]
# convention-card-ns: 21GF-DEFAULT
# convention-card-ew: 21GF-GIB

/*@chat
--- East opens a 4-level major preempt holding an 8+ card semi-solid heart or spade suit.
Semi-solid means two of the top three honors plus the jack or ten, with most of the
strength in the long suit and fewer than 11 HCP. North and South must decide whether to
double, bid on, or pass it out.
@chat*/

# Opps Preempt 4M 
dealer east

#include "script/Leveling"

tp = hcp(east)
sp = hcp(east,spades)
hp = hcp(east,hearts)

# Semi-solid: 2 of the top 3 honors plus at least one of the jack or ten
eS = spades(east)>7 and top3(east,spades)>1 and top5(east,spades)>2 and hearts(east)<4
eH = hearts(east)>7 and top3(east,hearts)>1 and top5(east,hearts)>2 and spades(east)<4

# Preemptive values -- most of the strength sits in the long suit
#sValues = eS and 2 * sp > tp
#hValues = eH and 2 * hp > tp

ePreempts = (eS or eH) and hcp(east)>6 and hcp(east)<11

# Thin out the exactly-8 card suits so the longer ones get some air
eight = spades(east)==8 or hearts(east)==8

ePreempts and (keep44 or not eight)

produce 40
action
average "4S opening   " 100 * eS,
average "4H opening   " 100 * eH,
average "8-card suit  " 100 * eight,
